# File: scripts/__tests__/extension-commands.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/464-run-nmg-sdlc-slash-commands-on-assigned-omp-model-roles/requirements.md
Feature: Run nmg-sdlc slash commands on assigned OMP model roles
  Automated nmg-sdlc file commands run on their OMP model role in the TUI,
  and the user's session model returns when the command's run ends.

  @SCN001
  Scenario: automated commands switch to their model role before the run
    Given an idle TUI session on model "test/main" with thinking level "medium"
    And the effective modelRoles are smol "test/fast:low" and slow "test/deep:xhigh"
    When the user submits "/sdlc-status", "/sdlc-open-pr #7", or "/sdlc-execute #7"
    Then before the input handler resolves the session model is "test/fast" with thinking level "low"
    And when the user submits "/sdlc-verify-code #7" the session model is "test/deep" with thinking level "xhigh"
    And when smol is "test/fast" without a suffix no thinking level is set by nmg-sdlc
    And the submitted text passes through unchanged for file-command expansion

  @SCN002
  Scenario: the prior model and thinking level return when the run ends
    Given "/sdlc-status" switched an idle TUI session from "test/main" at "medium" to "test/fast" at "low"
    When the command's run ends with completion, with an error stop, or with an aborted stop
    Then the session model is "test/main" with thinking level "medium"
    And an earlier agent_end with willContinue true restored nothing
    And setModel and setThinkingLevel were only called with a single argument and no modelRoles value was written

  @SCN003
  Scenario: a model or thinking choice made during the run is kept
    Given "/sdlc-verify-code #7" switched an idle TUI session from "test/main" at "medium" to "test/deep" at "xhigh"
    When the user selects model "test/other" or thinking level "high" before the run ends terminally
    Then after the run ends the user's selection is still active
    And "test/main" at "medium" is not restored

  @SCN004
  Scenario: interactive commands perform no model switch
    Given an idle TUI session on model "test/main" with thinking level "medium"
    When the user submits "/sdlc-draft-issue", "/sdlc-write-spec #7", "/sdlc-onboard-project", "/sdlc-upgrade-project", "/sdlc-steering", or "/sdlc-run-retro" and its run ends
    Then the input is rewritten to "/plan" followed by the workflow as before
    And nmg-sdlc made no setModel or setThinkingLevel call

  @SCN005
  Scenario: an unavailable role warns and continues on the current model
    Given an idle TUI session on model "test/main" with thinking level "medium"
    And "@slow" resolves to no available model, or to "test/locked" whose setModel returns false
    When the user submits "/sdlc-verify-code #7"
    Then the session stays on "test/main" with thinking level "medium"
    And the TUI shows the warning "NMG SDLC: @slow is unavailable; /sdlc-verify-code continues on the current model." once
    And the run's end restores nothing

  @SCN006
  Scenario: headless and busy sessions perform no model switch
    Given a session on model "test/main" with thinking level "medium"
    When "/sdlc-status" arrives with source "rpc", in a context without a TUI, or while the TUI session is streaming
    Then nmg-sdlc makes no setModel or setThinkingLevel call
    And the session model stays "test/main" with thinking level "medium"
